 PCL and PCLATH
The Program Counter is associated with two registers:
PCL (Program Counter Low): Contains the lower portion of the Program Counter.
PCLATH (Program Counter Latch): Provides the higher bits required for certain Program Counter operations.
These registers are important when implementing program-control instructions in the simulator.

